Initial implementation of the remote job execution system per SPEC.md: app models (JobDefinition, ExecutionZone, ZoneMembershipRule, Worker, WorkerEnrollmentToken, RemoteJobRun, RunArtifact, RemoteJobSchedule), zone resolution and dispatch with leases/reaper/retry, JSON-RPC control protocol with Redis gateway bridge, worker-facing REST API (enroll, logs, console, artifacts), per-run scoped tokens, guarded CancelFactory integration, dynamic run forms from JSON Schema, zone coverage report, Celery beat scheduler, and Kafka log consumer command. Mono-repo also ships the WebSocket gateway (gateway/), the worker agent (worker/), and the job SDK with `remote-jobs publish` CLI (sdk/).
